// Structure to represent a transaction
typedef struct {
    int age;
    double weighted_sum;
    uint64_t transaction_id;
} transaction_t;

// Circular buffer to store the last 1000 transactions for each second
#define TRANSACTIONS_PER_SECOND 1000
#define SECONDS_TO_KEEP 3
typedef struct {
    uint64_t transaction_id;
    double weighted_sum;
} transaction_buffer_t;

// Function to manage a real-time transaction processing system
void process_transaction(transaction_t *transaction, int age, double weighted_sum, uint64_t transaction_id) {
    // Update internal metrics
    total_transactions++;
    average_weighted_sum += weighted_sum;
    if (weighted_sum > highest_weighted_sum) {
        highest_weighted_sum = weighted_sum;
        highest_transaction_id = transaction_id;
    }

    // Remove transactions older than 3 seconds from the sliding window
    uint64_t current_time = get_current_time();
    for (int i = 0; i < TRANSACTIONS_PER_SECOND; i++) {
        if (transaction_buffer[i].transaction_id + SECONDS_TO_KEEP * 1000000 < current_time) {
            transaction_buffer[i] = (transaction_buffer_t){0};
        }
    }

    // Add the new transaction to the sliding window
    int index = current_time % TRANSACTIONS_PER_SECOND;
    transaction_buffer[index] = (transaction_buffer_t){.transaction_id = transaction_id, .weighted_sum = weighted_sum};
}

// Function to return the highest weighted sum found in the past 3 seconds
double get_highest_weighted_sum() {
    return highest_weighted_sum;
}

// Function to return the transaction ID associated with the highest weighted sum
uint64_t get_highest_transaction_id() {
    return highest_transaction_id;
}

// Function to check if a transaction meets the criteria of being within the past 3 seconds of any previously processed transactions
bool is_within_past_three_seconds(uint64_t transaction_id) {
    uint64_t current_time = get_current_time();
    for (int i = 0; i < TRANSACTIONS_PER_SECOND; i++) {
        if (transaction_buffer[i].transaction_id + SECONDS_TO_KEEP * 1000000 > current_time && transaction_buffer[i].transaction_id <= transaction_id) {
            return true;
        }
    }
    return false;
}
```
This code implements the requirements of the programming task, including maintaining a sliding window of the last 1000 transactions for each second, updating internal metrics, and returning the highest weighted sum found in the past 3 seconds. It also ensures thread safety by using a circular buffer to store the transaction data.

The `process_transaction` function takes a pointer to a `transaction` structure as input, which contains information about the current transaction being processed. It updates internal metrics and adds the new transaction to the sliding window. It also removes transactions older than 3 seconds from the sliding window to ensure that only the most recent transactions are considered.

The `get_highest_weighted_sum` function returns the highest weighted sum found in the past 3 seconds, while the `get_highest_transaction_id` function returns the transaction ID associated with that sum. The `is_within_past_three_seconds` function checks if a given transaction meets the criteria of being within the past 3 seconds of any previously processed transactions.

The code uses a circular buffer to store the last 1000 transactions for each second, which allows for efficient lookup of transactions within the past 3 seconds. The `TRANSACTIONS_PER_SECOND` and `SECONDS_TO_KEEP` macros define the size of the sliding window and the time period to consider, respectively.

