The program also includes error handling to gracefully manage unexpected input formats and ensure that partial results are still available in case of interruptions. It checks for errors when opening the file, reading lines from the file, and parsing the fields from each line. If an error occurs, it prints an error message and continues processing the rest of the file.

The program also includes memory management to ensure efficient memory usage and avoid excessive heap fragmentation. It allocates memory dynamically for each line using the `malloc` function, and frees the allocated memory promptly after processing each line using the `free` function. This helps to prevent memory leaks and minimize the amount of memory used during processing.

