Here is a Java method that loads a state object from a file, using an ObjectInputStream to read the object from the file and returning the object if it is an instance of the MoSTState class, else null. The method should handle exceptions and close the ObjectInputStream regardless of whether an exception is thrown.
```java
import java.io.*;

public static Object loadState(String filename) {
    try (ObjectInputStream ois = new ObjectInputStream(new FileInputStream(filename))) {
        Object obj = ois.readObject();
        if (obj instanceof MoSTState) {
            return obj;
        } else {
            return null;
        }
    } catch (IOException | ClassNotFoundException e) {
        System.out.println("Error loading state: " + e.getMessage());
        return null;
    } finally {
        try {
            ois.close();
        } catch (IOException e) {
            // ignore
        }
    }
}
