The function uses a custom allocator function instead of `malloc` and `free` to track allocations for debugging purposes. It also provides meaningful error codes if memory allocation fails or if the file operations encounter errors.

To ensure thread safety, the function uses mutexes provided by the standard library to manage access to the session data structure. The mutex is locked before any operation that modifies the session data structure, and it is unlocked after the operation is completed.

Finally, the function provides a mechanism to clean up all allocated resources and closed files when the function is done. This ensures no memory leaks or resource exhaustion occur.']

