log.addEntry(System.currentTimeMillis(), LogLevel.CRITICAL, "Critical message");
log.addEntry(System.currentTimeMillis(), LogLevel.INFO, "Informational message");
List<ModemLogEntry> entries = log.getEntriesByTimestamp(System.currentTimeMillis() - 1000);
for (ModemLogEntry entry : entries) {
  System.out.println(entry.getMessage());
}
log.clearLog();
log.setLogLevelFilter(LogLevel.CRITICAL);
List<ModemLogEntry> filteredEntries = log.getEntriesByTimestamp(System.currentTimeMillis() - 1000);
for (ModemLogEntry entry : filteredEntries) {
  System.out.println(entry.getMessage());
}
log.shutdown();
```
This code creates a new `ModemLog` instance, adds two log entries to the list, retrieves all log entries with a timestamp greater than or equal to the current time minus one second, clears the entire log, sets the log level filter to `CRITICAL`, and retrieves all log entries with a timestamp greater than or equal to the current time minus one second. Finally, it shuts down the executor service.

Note that this is just an example implementation, and you may need to modify it to fit your specific use case. Additionally, you should consider using a more robust logging library such as Log4j or SLF4J instead of implementing your own logging system from scratch.']

