The code uses a fixed-size array to store the TCP connection statistics, which is more efficient than dynamic memory allocation for large numbers of connections. The mutex `connections_mutex` is used to synchronize access to the connections array to prevent data corruption or race conditions when multiple threads access it concurrently.

The code also includes a mechanism to handle overflow by resizing the connections array when it becomes full. This ensures that the function can handle large numbers of connections without running out of memory.

