The `export_log()` function exports the log entries to a CSV file using the `fprintf()` function. It locks the mutex before accessing the log array and writes the header row of the CSV file followed by each entry in the log array. The `pthread_mutex_lock()` and `pthread_mutex_unlock()` functions are used to ensure thread safety when modifying the log array.

