The `LoadResourceBundle` function is used to load a resource bundle from a file, where each item is preceded by a header containing its size in bytes and type identifier. The function allocates memory dynamically for the entire bundle structure and ensures that all items are correctly parsed. It handles file operations, parsing errors, and memory allocation failures with robust error handling.

The `Get` function retrieves a `MAC_PDU` entry from the array based on its header value. If the entry is not found in the cache, it compresses the payload data using the `Compress` function and adds the compressed data to the cache. The `Insert` function inserts a new `MAC_PDU` entry into the array, evicting an existing entry if necessary to maintain data structure integrity. The `Remove` function removes an existing `MAC_PDU` entry from the array based on its header value.

The `Compress` and `Decompress` functions use the `DeflateStream` class to compress and decompress data, respectively. They take advantage of the `COMPRESSION_LEVEL` constant to control the compression level.

The `DynamicArrayManager` class is designed to be thread-safe, ensuring efficient handling of large files without exhausting system resources. It also integrates with an external data source to fetch a list of predefined ranges that it can draw from, enhancing the flexibility of the class.']

