The `flush_log` function writes the entire log array to a file on disk, while the `archive_logs` function calculates the age of the oldest entry in the log and archives it if it is older than a specified duration. The `handle_concurrent_access` function creates a cache for recently accessed log entries to improve performance when multiple threads access the log array simultaneously.

The code also defines several constants for configuring the maximum size of the log array, the frequency at which logs are flushed to disk, and the duration for which logs are kept before being archived. These constants can be adjusted as needed to optimize performance and memory usage.']

