```
This class represents a single request in the cache, with an ID, metadata, and an expiration time. The `setExpirationTime` method is used to set the expiration time for the request, which is used by the cache to determine when a request is stale and should be evicted.

The `Metadata` class is defined as follows:
```cpp
class Metadata {
public:
    // Constructor
    Metadata(const std::string& key, const std::string& value) :
        _key(key),
        _value(value) {}

    // Getter for the key
    const std::string& getKey() const {
        return _key;
    }

    // Getter for the value
    const std::string& getValue() const {
        return _value;
    }

    // Check if a metadata matches a given criteria
