The function uses a semaphore to synchronize access to the dynamic array, ensuring that only one thread can modify it at a time. It also includes a mechanism for handling errors and recovering from them, as well as a strategy for handling edge cases such as invalid RNTI values or missing CRC indication tags.

The function also includes a mechanism for monitoring the performance of the dynamic array management, generating periodic reports on memory usage, throughput, and error rates. These reports are accessible via a custom API endpoint, allowing for real-time monitoring and debugging.

Finally, the function supports asynchronous updates to the dynamic array, ensuring that modifications are consistent across all threads without disrupting ongoing operations.']

